===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of or pertaining to the north; [[northern]].
#: ''He lived in '''north''' Germany''.
#: ''She entered through the '''north''' gate.''
# Toward the north; [[northward]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1987|author=Ana María Brull Vázquez|author2=Rosa E. Casas|title=Cuba|page=23
|passage=The most dangerous ones are those that develop during October and November and that follow a '''north''' path affecting the western part of the island.}}
# {{lb|en|meteorology}} Of wind, from the north.
#: ''The '''north''' wind was cold.''
# Pertaining to the part of a [[corridor]] used by [[northbound]] [[traffic]].
#: '''''north''' highway 1''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Joseph R Miller|title=Pipe Tobacco and Wool|passage=Traffic was doing the speed limit on '''North''' I-45 one minute and had come to a stand-still the next.}}
# {{lb|en|ecclesiastical}} Designating, or situated in, the liturgical north (in a church, the direction to the left-hand side of a person facing the [[altar]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Michael Attridge|author2=Catherine E. Clifford|author3=Gilles Routhier|title=Vatican II: Expériences canadiennes – Canadian experiences|publisher=University of Ottawa Press|isbn=9782760319523|page=145
|passage={{...}} the high church had liked its clergy to preside at the Eucharist in an ''ad orientem'' position; the low church advocated what was called the '''north''' end position; but the Liturgical Movement asked the priest to take a basilical position, facing liturgical west, and now both Anglican factions could agree on this third position without either of them losing face.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Paul Porwoll|title=Against All Odds: History of Saint Andrew's Parish Church, Charleston, 1706-2013|publisher=WestBow Press|isbn=9781490818177|page=365
|passage=Throughout the book I refer directionally to the altar and chancel of St. Andrew&#39;s as situated at ''ecclesiastical'' east (to avoid overcomplicating matters), not ''geographical'' or ''magnetic'' southeast. Thus, {{...}} The '''north''' side faces the river (beyond the subdivision behind the church), and the south side, Ashley River Road. {{...}} At St. Andrew's, ecclesiastical north, south, east, and west correspond to geographical northeast, southwest, southeast, and northwest. Unless otherwise indicated, compass directions given in this book are ecclesiastical, not geographical, reference points.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} More or greater than.
#: ''The wedding ended up costing '''north''' of $50,000.''
#* {{quote-av|en|1993|Tom Aldredge|[[w:Barbarians at the Gate (film)|Barbarians at the Gate]]|role=Charlie Hugel|passage=The price you're offering had better be '''north''' of the highest price this company has ever traded for.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=Dec 2021|journal= The Road Ahead|place=Brisbane|page=57|column=2|text=Some of the windscreens we replace cost '''north''' of $1800[.]}}

